        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "text": "2 The brief facts of the case as per record and from trial court record are that accused is running an establishment namely M/s Tandoori Nights, 153, Main Road, Jheel, Delhi.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 672,
      "end": 846,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Delhi",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 840,
          "end": 845
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.07349280267953873
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 6,
      "text": "On 26.05.2003 at about 3.30 p.m. Food Inspector Sh. Ranjeet Singh visited the said place and purchased 1500 grams of \"Dal Arhar\" from accused.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 847,
      "end": 989,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "26.05.2003",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 850,
          "end": 860
        },
        {
          "text": "Ranjeet Singh",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 899,
          "end": 912
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.20865611732006073
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "FI was accompanied with SDM/LHA Sh. C. P. Sharma.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 990,
      "end": 1039,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "C. P. Sharma",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 1026,
          "end": 1038
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.12691906094551086
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "The said Arhar Dal was purchased for the CA No. 09/16 Rajesh Batra Vs. State page 1 of 6 purposes of analysis under PFA Act.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1040,
      "end": 1164,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Arhar Dal",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 1049,
          "end": 1058
        },
        {
          "text": "CA No. 09/16 Rajesh Batra Vs. State",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 1081,
          "end": 1116
        },
        {
          "text": "PFA Act",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1156,
          "end": 1163
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.26943522691726685
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "The same sample was divided into three parts, packed as per Rules of PFA.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1165,
      "end": 1238,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "PFA",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1234,
          "end": 1237
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.23929356038570404
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "Panchanama was prepared.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1239,
      "end": 1263,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.17854420840740204
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "One sample was sent for analysis to Public Analyst.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1264,
      "end": 1315,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.25460612773895264
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "As per the report of Analyst, sample did not confirm to the standard because \"The sample is adulterated because it is coloured with synthetic colouring matter viz. Tartrazine.\"",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1316,
      "end": 1492,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.21405918896198273
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "3 As the sample was failed, prosecution was launched by Food Inspector by filing complaint dated 08.09.2004 with the court.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1494,
      "end": 1617,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "08.09.2004",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 1591,
          "end": 1601
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.39235928654670715
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 14,
      "text": "Accused was summoned.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1618,
      "end": 1639,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.257196307182312
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 15,
      "text": "He has exercised his right u/sec.13(2) PFA Act to get the sample analyzed by CFL.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1640,
      "end": 1721,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "sec.13(2)",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 1669,
          "end": 1678
        },
        {
          "text": "PFA Act",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1679,
          "end": 1686
        },
        {
          "text": "CFL",
          "label": "ORG",
          "start": 1717,
          "end": 1720
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.34043586254119873
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 16,
      "text": "CFL reported \"I am of the opinion that the sample bearing no.\n21/LHA/6225 does not conform to standards of split pulse (Dal) Arhar as per PFA Rules, 1955 Sh. Rajesh Batra vs The State (Delhi Administration) on 14 May, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/120084627/\n1 (Synthetic colour Tartrazine detected), Weelvilled grains are found 8.6% (standard not more than 3%) and uric acid content 685.4 PPM (not more than 100 mg per kilogram).\"\n4",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 1722,
      "end": 2174,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "CFL",
          "label": "ORG",
          "start": 1722,
          "end": 1725
        },
        {
          "text": "14 May, 2016",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 1932,
          "end": 1944
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.1663224995136261
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 17,
      "text": "Charge was framed against accused u/sec.2(ia) (a) (j) (m) read with sec.7 of PFA Act, 1954 punishable u/sec.16(1A) of PFA Act.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 2175,
      "end": 2301,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "sec.2(ia) (a) (j) (m) read with sec.7",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 2211,
          "end": 2248
        },
        {
          "text": "PFA Act, 1954",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 2252,
          "end": 2265
        },
        {
          "text": "sec.16(1A)",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 2279,
          "end": 2289
        },
        {
          "text": "PFA Act",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 2293,
          "end": 2300
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.5804142951965332
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 18,
      "text": "5 After trial, vide judgment dated 24.02.2014 accused was convicted for offence u/sec.16(1A) of PFA Act and vide order on sentence dated 06.03.2014, accused was directed to undergo simple imprisonment for a period of 18 months and fine of Rs.10,000/- and in default of payment of fine SI of 30 days.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RLC",
      "start": 2302,
      "end": 2602,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "24.02.2014",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 2338,
          "end": 2348
        },
        {
          "text": "sec.16(1A)",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 2385,
          "end": 2395
        },
        {
          "text": "PFA Act",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 2399,
          "end": 2406
        },
        {
          "text": "06.03.2014",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 2440,
          "end": 2450
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.21607328951358795
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 19,
      "text": "6 In this appeal, the accused has assailed the judgment on the following grounds:-",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 2603,
      "end": 2687,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.15795160830020905
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 20,
      "text": "( i) The commodity i.e. Dal Arhar was not for sale but was for private consumption by the employees of the accused.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ISSUE",
      "start": 2687,
      "end": 2802,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Dal Arhar",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 2711,
          "end": 2720
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "issue",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.2807892858982086
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 21,
      "text": "CA No. 09/16 Rajesh Batra Vs. State page 2 of 6 (ii) There is variation in different reports (PA and CFL) so the sample was not properly homogenized.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 2803,
      "end": 2953,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "CA No. 09/16 Rajesh Batra Vs. State",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 2804,
          "end": 2839
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.20726025104522705
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 22,
      "text": "(iii) Percentage of colour not mentioned in report.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 2954,
      "end": 3006,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.12607572972774506
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 23,
      "text": "(iv) Violation of Rule 17 and 18.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 3007,
      "end": 3041,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Rule 17",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 3026,
          "end": 3033
        },
        {
          "text": "18",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 3038,
          "end": 3040
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.16096600890159607
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 24,
      "text": "(v) Non-compliance of Rule 14 of PFA Rules i.e. the bottles, spoon etc. were not made clean and dried at the spot by the food inspector or any other official.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 3042,
      "end": 3201,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Rule 14",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 3065,
          "end": 3072
        },
        {
          "text": "PFA Rules",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 3076,
          "end": 3085
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.1503990739583969
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 25,
      "text": "7 No reply was filed by respondent/state and the matter was argued orally.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 3202,
      "end": 3277,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.08324223756790161
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 26,
      "text": "8 I have gone through the record, Trial Court record and have heard the submissions of Ld. counsel for appellant and Ld. SPP for State.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 3279,
      "end": 3414,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 27,
      "text": "9 It is argued by Ld. counsel for accused that Dal Arhar was not for sale but for the private consumption of the employees of the accused.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 3416,
      "end": 3554,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Dal Arhar",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 3463,
          "end": 3472
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.06727538257837296
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 28,
      "text": "It is stated that due to that reason no amount was taken from the FI.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 3555,
      "end": 3624,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.07163392007350922
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 29,
      "text": "This leg of argument is dealt by the trial court from para 27 to 36.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 3625,
      "end": 3693,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.04488273337483406
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 30,
      "text": "I do not find any other opinion than that given by the trial court and thus the finding of the trial court in this regard is upheld.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 3694,
      "end": 3826,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.04582035914063454
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 31,
      "text": "10 It is further stated that there is variation in the report of PA and CFL and due to that reason benefit goes in favour of the accused.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 3828,
      "end": 3965,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.06884513050317764
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 32,
      "text": "This line of argument was done before the trial court and was dealt in para 55 to 91 of the judgment.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 3966,
      "end": 4067,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.08011027425527573
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 33,
      "text": "I do not want to differ from the reasoning given by the trial court and thus the same is upheld.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4068,
      "end": 4164,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.025920605286955833
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 34,
      "text": "Sh. Rajesh Batra vs The State (Delhi Administration) on 14 May, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/120084627/\n2 11",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 4165,
      "end": 4294,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Rajesh Batra vs The State (Delhi Administration)",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 4170,
          "end": 4218
        },
        {
          "text": "14 May, 2016",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 4222,
          "end": 4234
        },
        {
          "text": "Indian Kanoon",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 4235,
          "end": 4248
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 35,
      "text": "It is further argued that compliance u/sec.14, 17 and 18 PFA Rules was not proved on record by the prosecution.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4295,
      "end": 4406,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "sec.14",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 4334,
          "end": 4340
        },
        {
          "text": "17",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 4342,
          "end": 4344
        },
        {
          "text": "18",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 4349,
          "end": 4351
        },
        {
          "text": "PFA Rules",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 4352,
          "end": 4361
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.12358670681715012
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 36,
      "text": "It is CA No. 09/16",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4407,
      "end": 4425,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "CA No. 09/16",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 4413,
          "end": 4425
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.07410761713981628
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 37,
      "text": "Rajesh Batra Vs. State  witnesses are deposing differently with respect to the cleanliness of spoon etc.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4426,
      "end": 4530,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Rajesh Batra Vs. State",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 4426,
          "end": 4448
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.12428200989961624
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 38,
      "text": "It is further stated that it was the duty of the prosecution to prove these facts.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4531,
      "end": 4613,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.04826393723487854
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 39,
      "text": "These arguments were also addressed before the trial court.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4614,
      "end": 4673,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.04524542763829231
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 40,
      "text": "The relevant part of the judgment dealing with these arguments are from para 37 to 64 of the judgment.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4674,
      "end": 4776,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.017914341762661934
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 41,
      "text": "12 As far as the arguments in this regard is concerned, the law discussed by the trial court is correct and the same is self explanatory.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4778,
      "end": 4915,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.04984774440526962
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 42,
      "text": "However, as far as the analysis of facts are concerned, to my opinion, the same requires some more elaboration.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 4916,
      "end": 5027,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.041904449462890625
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 43,
      "text": "13 As far as Rule 14 of PFA Rules are concerned, it spells out that the FI shall use dry bottles or containers for the purposes of sampling.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 5029,
      "end": 5169,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Rule 14",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 5042,
          "end": 5049
        },
        {
          "text": "PFA Rules",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 5053,
          "end": 5062
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.23101964592933655
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 44,
      "text": "However, this fact was elaborated further by Hon. Supreme Court in Varghese Vs. Food, 1989 (II) Prevention of Food Adulteration Cases, 236 stating that \"it must be the endeavour of the FI to use clean and dry implements in sampling the articles of food.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
      "start": 5170,
      "end": 5423,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Supreme Court",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 5220,
          "end": 5233
        },
        {
          "text": "Varghese Vs. Food, 1989 (II) Prevention of Food Adulteration Cases, 236",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 5237,
          "end": 5308
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.14201892912387848
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 45,
      "text": "If unhygienic methods are adopted, it will effect the result of analysis.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
      "start": 5424,
      "end": 5497,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.0791550725698471
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 46,
      "text": "So, the Hon. Supreme Court use the word \"implements\" instead of only \"dry and clean bottles/containers\".",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
      "start": 5498,
      "end": 5602,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Supreme Court",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 5511,
          "end": 5524
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.07515913248062134
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 47,
      "text": "Similarly, in other judgments, i.e. State of Haryana Vs. Kishan Kumar CLT 559, it was observed that the prosecution had not stated that the \"weighing scale\" was clean.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
      "start": 5603,
      "end": 5770,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "State of Haryana Vs. Kishan Kumar CLT 559",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 5639,
          "end": 5680
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.27094703912734985
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 48,
      "text": "Similarly, in other judgments, like Sardar Mal Jain, 1996 (2) Prevention of Food Adulteration Cases, 203, it was stated that the newspaper on which the Barfi was weighed was not clean.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
      "start": 5771,
      "end": 5955,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Sardar Mal Jain, 1996 (2) Prevention of Food Adulteration Cases, 203",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 5807,
          "end": 5875
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.06719419360160828
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 49,
      "text": "Similarly, in Shashi Kant Vs. State of UP, 1983 (1)\nPrevention of Food Adulteration Cases 90, it was observed that the \"bhagona\" was not proved to be clean and dry.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
      "start": 5956,
      "end": 6120,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Shashi Kant Vs. State of UP, 1983 (1)\nPrevention of Food Adulteration Cases 90",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 5970,
          "end": 6048
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.332845002412796
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 50,
      "text": "CA No. 09/16 Rajesh Batra Vs. State  14",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
      "start": 6121,
      "end": 6161,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Rajesh Batra Vs. State",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 6135,
          "end": 6157
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.4327569007873535
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 51,
      "text": "So, accordingly, it can be said that the law which can be crystallized from various judgments of Hon. High Courts as well as Hon. Supreme Court is that if in evidence, the prosecution states that the sample commodity had touched a surface of an \"implement\" or any other surface, it is the duty of the prosecution to prove beyond reasonable doubt that the said implement/surface was clean and dry and thus could not have added any impurity to the sample.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
      "start": 6162,
      "end": 6615,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Supreme Court",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 6292,
          "end": 6305
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.366606742143631
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 52,
      "text": "However, it is not the law that the FI shall spell out on which surfaces the sample commodity had touched while sampling.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 6616,
      "end": 6737,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.6143300533294678
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 53,
      "text": "However, if he chooses to spell out the implements/surfaces with which the sample commodity came into contact/touch, the same must be proved as clean and dry.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 6738,
      "end": 6896,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.6270236968994141
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 54,
      "text": "Sh. Rajesh Batra vs The State (Delhi Administration) on 14 May, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/120084627/\n3 15",
      "rhetorical_role": "PRE_RELIED",
      "start": 6897,
      "end": 7026,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Rajesh Batra vs The State (Delhi Administration)",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 6902,
          "end": 6950
        },
        {
          "text": "14 May, 2016",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 6954,
          "end": 6966
        },
        {
          "text": "Indian Kanoon",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 6967,
          "end": 6980
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.4252103269100189
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 55,
      "text": "In the present case, neither PW1 nor PW2 had stated anything about as to how the Dal was weighed.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 7027,
      "end": 7124,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3985542356967926
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 56,
      "text": "However, PW3 in his cross-examination deposed that it was weighed on an electronic balance.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 7125,
      "end": 7216,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.183406800031662
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 57,
      "text": "The electronic balance was kept by the vendor for weighing the food articles like Dal, spices etc.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 7217,
      "end": 7315,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.5431962013244629
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 58,
      "text": "Now no where prosecution had deposed that this electronic balance was clean and dry and free from any colour.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 7316,
      "end": 7425,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3351733386516571
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 59,
      "text": "Thus there is violation of Rule 14 of PFA Rules.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 7426,
      "end": 7474,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Rule 14",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 7453,
          "end": 7460
        },
        {
          "text": "PFA Rules",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 7464,
          "end": 7473
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.6016449332237244
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 60,
      "text": "16 So, in these circumstances, the prosecution failed to prove the strict compliance u/sec.14 of PFA Rules.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 7476,
      "end": 7583,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "sec.14",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 7563,
          "end": 7569
        },
        {
          "text": "PFA Rules",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 7573,
          "end": 7582
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.5261563658714294
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 61,
      "text": "17 So, the judgment and order on sentence of the trial court is reversed.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 7585,
      "end": 7658,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3208881616592407
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 62,
      "text": "18 Accused Rajesh Batra is acquitted of the charges u/sec.16(1A) read with sec.7 of PFA Act.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 7660,
      "end": 7752,
      "entities": [
